%% The transaction flow as implemented today: a single node, one transaction per
%% block, with the ledger written before any in-memory state changes.
%% For the target multi-node flow, see the Consensus Layer notes in architecture.mmd.
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant CLI as CLI / Explorer
    participant Wallet
    participant RPC as JSON-RPC
    participant Mempool
    participant State
    participant Storage as Ledger

    User->>CLI: subhost tx send
    CLI->>Wallet: decrypt key (scrypt + AES-256-GCM)
    Wallet-->>CLI: ed25519 signing key
    CLI->>RPC: eth_chainId, eth_getTransactionCount
    RPC-->>CLI: chain ID, next nonce
    CLI->>CLI: sign the unsigned encoding (ed25519)
    CLI->>RPC: eth_sendTransaction + publicKey + signature

    RPC->>RPC: verify signature; public key must hash to `from`
    RPC->>RPC: check chain ID and gas limit

    alt Signature or parameters invalid
        RPC-->>CLI: JSON-RPC error -32602
        CLI-->>User: rejected, nothing changed
    else Accepted into the pool
        RPC->>Mempool: admit (replace-by-fee, capacity, budget)
        RPC->>State: apply_transaction on a state clone

        alt Nonce, balance, or type rejected
            State-->>RPC: StateError
            RPC->>Mempool: roll back, restoring any displaced tx
            RPC-->>CLI: JSON-RPC error -32000
            CLI-->>User: rejected, nothing changed
        else Executed
            RPC->>RPC: seal a one-tx block (tx_root, receipt_root, state_root)
            RPC->>Storage: persist state + blocks + receipts atomically

            alt Persist failed
                Storage-->>RPC: StorageError
                RPC->>Mempool: roll back
                RPC-->>CLI: JSON-RPC error -32603
                CLI-->>User: rejected, disk and memory still agree
            else Committed
                Storage-->>RPC: fsynced
                RPC->>State: swap in the new state
                RPC->>Mempool: remove the mined tx
                RPC-->>CLI: transaction hash
                CLI-->>User: hash of a committed block
            end
        end
    end

    Note over RPC,Storage: No peer propagation and no consensus.<br/>Production is single-node.
